# Do not undo earlier fixes

The code on disk is the last behavior the user asked for, including uncommitted edits. A new request changes only what it names.

Before editing a file, read the function you will touch, then `git diff -- <file>` and `git log -5 -- <file>`. Uncommitted lines stay.

- Patch the lines the request needs. Do not rewrite the surrounding function, QML item, or rule from memory.
- A failed search-replace means the file differs from what you expected. Read it again. Do not replace the whole block, and do not treat the failed edit as done.
- Do not restyle, rename, move, or remove a neighboring control, overlay, menu, scrollbar, button size, or theme token.
- Do not delete telescope album files except the ones the user named.
- If an attempt fails, remove that attempt before finishing. Do not leave the workaround in the tree.

These stay unless this request names them:

- Neighbor-fill panel resize, and the pane sizes the user set across maximize and restore
- Wide-view taps as Dual Lenses Locating in `1920x1080`, with no PictureMatching offset on the command
- Mosaic overlap, dotted frames, tele-only panes and STACK MOSAIC, ICRS pane numbers, and the contact sheet kept until live view
- Auto Parameters kept across PHOTO and DSO until a manual exposure, gain, or stack count is saved
- Panorama framing on the wide camera. Do not resize the tele field. Shot count changes only through the framing rectangle the user set
- Sky-map load path and restore of the last RA/Dec
- Preview only for live view. Polar alignment does not start it. Disconnect stops it
- The first custom-mosaic pane keeps calibrate, focus, polar alignment, and the waits. Later panes only slew and stack
- Deleting a history row removes the history file and leaves the session in place
- The scheduler due list is tonight only. Earlier nights stay planned
- Setup focuses the field already in frame. Polar positioning runs only when the session calibrates. A failed autofocus retries after calibration
- A user stop is Stopped by user, skips remaining mosaic panes before the worker returns, and does not chain the next pane
- Do not send another GOTO while `goto_released` is set. Wait for `goto_search_cleared`
- A running mosaic keeps its saved pane centres on the chart (`fixed_panes`)

Before finishing, read `git diff` for every file touched. Put back any line the request did not ask for.
